Position-synchronized moves must not run through the jerk-limited planner.

G33 and G33.1 track the spindle every cycle with a correction sized for an
acceleration that changes at once. With PLANNER_TYPE = 1 the delay of the jerk
limit made Z oscillate around the spindle, and Ruckig refused the zero velocity
the tracking loop sometimes asks for ("invalid limits (v=0.000000, ...)").

Checks, at servo rate, that Z runs smoothly during G33 and G33.1, that the
message does not appear, and that an unsynchronized move is still jerk limited.
